cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code, please cite the archived release you used."
title: "Ascarid-Molecular-Evolution: code for the molecular evolution of genes removed by programmed DNA elimination in ascarid nematodes"
abstract: >-
  Python and shell code for the molecular evolution of genes removed by
  programmed DNA elimination in four ascarid nematodes (Ascaris, Parascaris
  univalens, Baylisascaris schroederi and Toxocara canis): pairwise and
  branch-specific dN/dS, constraint around chromosomal breakage regions, codon
  usage, gene structure, chromatin context, and polymorphism in an Ascaris
  population sample.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Simmons
    given-names: James R.
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0888-1151"
    affiliation: "Department of Biochemistry & Cellular and Molecular Biology, University of Tennessee, Knoxville"
repository-code: "https://github.com/jsimmo45/Ascarid-Molecular-Evolution"
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
keywords:
  - programmed DNA elimination
  - molecular evolution
  - dN/dS
  - relaxed selection
  - polymorphism
  - nematodes
  - Ascaris
